// amp_cuda_to_hip.inc -- CUDA name -> HIP name, #define per symbol.
// Extracted from CUDA_IDENTIFIER_MAP / CUDA_TYPE_NAME_MAP / friends in
// torch/utils/hipify/cuda_to_hip_mappings.py of the torch-2.9.1+rocm6.4
// wheel (every plain identifier -> identifier pair regardless of which
// CUDA library family it's tagged under -- runtime, driver, BLAS, SPARSE,
// RAND, FFT; cheaper to carry a few hundred unused #defines than to
// chase missing ones one compile error at a time). A handful of entries
// hipify's table doesn't carry (used by this project's own code, not by
// libtorch's headers) are appended by hand.
//
// Included by the forwarding headers in this directory, which stand in
// for a real cuda*.h on the -I path: libtorch's ROCm wheel ships its
// public headers verbatim from the CUDA build (hipify only rewrites the
// .cpp/.cu translation units that go into the wheel's .so, not the
// installed header tree), so they still say e.g. `#include <cusparse.h>`
// and expect the including project to provide one -- which is what a
// real CUDA toolkit normally does, and ROCm does not.
